WEBVTT

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:08.150
Lupin III...

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:11.180
Real name: unknown. 
Family and background: unknown.

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:14.520
There are claims that his grandfather 
was the infamous thief, Arsène Lupin,

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:17.200
but there's no proof to 
back up these assertions.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:21.610
Just looking at the data, it's hard 
to tell whether he even exists...

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:24.870
Doesn't that make him perfect, though?

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:28.750
A celebrity targeted by 
police the world over,

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.670
who is also the most 
enigmatic man on the planet.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:35.150
You know what they call people like that?

00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:37.250
I don't know. Ghosts?

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:41.020
No. Heroes.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:07.940
<b>The Girl in the Twin Towers</b>

00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:18.690
<i>Rennais has the ball as it goes from from Mexer to Prcić!</i>

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:21.700
<i>Prcić is marauding forward
up the left wing!</i>

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:25.450
<i>Wow! Djidji manages to get between
 him and the ball for the steal!</i>

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:28.740
<i>It then goes to Rongier and then 
Gillet on the right of the field.</i>

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:30.210
<i>He slips through and fires off a shot!</i>

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:31.570
<i>But the keeper saves it!</i>

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:34.480
<i>What a miss!</i>

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:34.160
So close!

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:37.520
Goddammit! How d'you 
miss a sitter like that?!

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:41.600
That's like your girl telling you she's good 
to go, but still finding a way to strikeout!

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:42.280
Ugh...

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:45.210
And you call yourself a man?! Sheesh.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:49.050
Looks like I won the bet.

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:51.870
Hey, shut your mouth! 
There's still the second half to go!

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:00.830
One moment, please...

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:05.090
Sorry about that. What with the 
stairs and being on the fourth floor...

00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:07.890
What's in the package?

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:09.650
Drugs.

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:10.750
What?!

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:12.780
Yup, all here.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:15.750
They send drugs in the mail now?

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:18.070
Not just drugs.

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:23.300
Guns, women, cash... you can get 
anything on the internet these days.

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:27.540
Looks like the stuff's legit.

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:40.500
If you dig deep enough on the internet, 
you'll find an online store called Marco Polo.

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:43.270
And their merch is the real deal?

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:46.290
A glance at their customer reviews...

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:49.320
is usually all it takes to confirm 
if a place is delivering.

00:03:50.050 --> 00:03:52.680
It's safer and more reliable
than buying from the mafia,

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:55.030
and their secure payment system 
has no third-party involvement.

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:57.720
Cheap, fast, and convenient!

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:01.350
Thanks to these guys, a third of the drugs in
circulation right now are distributed online.

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:04.080
Here you are.

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:06.210
Ah, that's the stuff.

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:11.720
We basically rented this room
because of you and these galettes.

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:15.110
I'm glad the two of you enjoy the food here.

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:19.890
Yum! We should've come 
down here in the first place.

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:24.690
You're the one who was glued to the TV.

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:25.970
Enjoy!

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:31.730
So this time, this Marco Polo 
place is the target?

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:35.860
All their deals are done digitally.

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:38.920
So we're gonna swoop in 
and snatch all that dough.

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:44.440
Something doesn't sit right with me about 
stealing something you can't touch.

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:48.010
Digital currency or cold, 
hard cash: it's all the same.

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:52.150
Even down to the fact that you 
always need a key to open the safe.

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:03.060
We're heading for the cloud data center.

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:07.200
A massive server bank that was put together 
by a bunch of defense contractors.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:09.180
Also known as the Twin Towers.

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:10.790
"Twin"?

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.480
I only see one.

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:15.280
The other one's down there.

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:17.540
In the ocean, huh?

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:22.080
Go down 128 meters and you'll find 
the manager's residential block.

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:25.030
The resident of that block 
is the one who has our key.

00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:27.340
That's pretty damn deep.

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:30.190
We dealin' with a moleman here? 
Actually, a mermaid's more likely.

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:33.770
The only ocean this "mermaid" 
swims in is a cyber one, though.

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:35.600
A hacker?

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:39.060
Apparently, this individual put 
together Marco Polo's payment system.

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:45.320
"Thieves are in the shadows. 
All's right with the world."

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:47.550
Run infiltration tools...

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:51.260
Access as an administrator.

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:04.230
Isn't the key gonna be underwater?

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:06.780
The people guarding it probably are, too.

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:08.330
So first, we go up.

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:22.600
They cool the servers with seawater.

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:35.230
I only mess with blades 
when I'm shaving...

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:37.230
Oh, hold your horses.

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:42.650
How long's it gonna be off?

00:06:42.650 --> 00:06:43.730
Fifteen seconds.

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:44.580
Plenty of time.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:47.910
Let's do this!

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:18.750
Lupin!

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:58.770
And here we are, 128 meters below sea level!

00:07:58.770 --> 00:08:00.790
The manager's residential block!

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:03.280
What's with the getup?

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:06.800
I'm gonna pretend to be family 
to try to get close to our hacker friend.

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:12.800
Man, does someone seriously live down here?

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:16.700
Yeah. The lease was set up five years ago.

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:55.940
A girl?

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:07.930
Who are you?

00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:11.700
Oh, my dear Amy!

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:13.170
I'm your father!

00:09:13.710 --> 00:09:15.960
But I suppose you don't remember me...

00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:20.150
You were so little back then.

00:09:20.150 --> 00:09:22.190
Wrong...

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:25.310
It's Ami, not Amy.

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:31.230
Wh-Whoa! Cut that out!

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:33.130
Whoa! Whoa!

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:34.540
You all right, Lupin?!

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:37.080
That was close! Not even a word of warning!

00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:41.720
Hello, Underworld.

00:09:45.190 --> 00:09:47.440
Run IDS sniffer.

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:49.980
Analyze any unauthorized 
access in the logs.

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:52.440
Transmit intruder data to security.

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:56.870
What's with this girl? Is she a robot?

00:09:56.870 --> 00:09:59.130
It's the same tech as my monocle.

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:01.860
She probably had the gear
 surgically implanted, though.

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:06.020
Who are they?!

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:07.740
When did they sneak in?!

00:10:08.190 --> 00:10:12.000
Hey, I thought you'd hacked the security 
system so they wouldn't notice us!

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:14.360
Someone's flushed us out.

00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:15.250
Which means...

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:19.500
She's the real deal.

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:22.060
<i>Intruders in the underwater 
manager's residence!</i>

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:23.790
<i>Response team, mobilize immediately!</i>

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:26.300
<i>Eliminate the intruders on sight!</i>

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:29.280
Her aim was all over the place.

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:30.850
She's an amateur with that piece.

00:10:30.850 --> 00:10:33.410
She won't hit you unless 
you're at point-blank range.

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:34.620
I thought as much.

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:36.020
Have you figured it out yet?

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:37.920
She's a smart cookie.

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:40.850
It might've looked like she was shooting 
wildly, but she's left herself some ammo.

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:44.790
A Baby Browning holds six rounds.

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:46.630
She's got one bullet left.

00:10:46.630 --> 00:10:48.400
I'll head back in, then.

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:49.530
Hey, Lupin!

00:10:50.030 --> 00:10:54.300
Sorry about all that 
"I'm your father" stuff before!

00:10:57.200 --> 00:10:58.650
You don't think I'll shoot?

00:10:58.650 --> 00:11:00.450
You couldn't if you wanted to.

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:01.320
Why not?

00:11:01.880 --> 00:11:04.500
Because I'm actually a prophet.

00:11:07.840 --> 00:11:10.730
Great. Here come the professionals.

00:11:14.660 --> 00:11:17.350
Lupin, I can't hold out here for long.

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:22.370
If my prophecy is right, then you'll 
tell me about Marco Polo's backdoor.

00:11:22.810 --> 00:11:25.450
Search: 26 ACP.

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:27.360
Display velocity and lethality summary.

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:34.870
You built the system, so I'm sure 
you put in a secret way to get into it.

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:38.120
I warned you.

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:45.660
Sorry about lying again...

00:11:46.070 --> 00:11:50.650
You see, I'm actually a thief.

00:11:52.990 --> 00:11:56.620
Access security footage from 
Camera 24. Six minutes ago.

00:11:56.620 --> 00:11:58.980
<i>But I suppose you don't remember me...</i>

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:02.700
<i>You were so little back then.</i>

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:03.610
Reduce speed.

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:12.790
Let me introduce myself officially...

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:15.540
I'm Lupin III. A thief.

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:18.250
An exquisitely skilled one, I might add.

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:19.630
And you can steal anything?

00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:22.000
Other than a woman's tears.

00:12:24.210 --> 00:12:26.970
Execute 0-D attack on facility's 
management systems.

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:31.930
What's going on?!

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:36.930
You've got a deal, Lupin III.

00:12:36.930 --> 00:12:39.340
You tell me about the backdoor...

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:42.400
And what do you want me to steal in return?

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:43.940
Me.

00:12:46.430 --> 00:12:49.610
There are invisible chains 
keeping me here...

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:56.470
Consider it done. I'm an old hand at 
spiriting away melancholy young ladies.

00:13:13.030 --> 00:13:14.970
Jigen, your path is clear.

00:13:14.970 --> 00:13:19.580
Would it have killed you to 
take 'em down a bit sooner, Goemon?

00:13:32.610 --> 00:13:35.190
Are you sure that tablet's where 
you want to focus your attention?

00:13:36.550 --> 00:13:39.370
Do you know what the deep web is?

00:13:39.370 --> 00:13:41.040
What is it? Some kind of music?

00:13:41.780 --> 00:13:45.450
You could say that. The kind 
that makes you really happy...

00:13:45.450 --> 00:13:46.790
What the hell?!

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:54.060
What do you mean?

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:56.100
I'm talking about 
Marco Polo!!

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:57.600
The ledger's
 been altered!!!!!

00:13:57.600 --> 00:13:58.650
(Mad)(Mad)(Mad)!!!!!!

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:00.110
N-Not good...

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:01.110
My admin access
 has been revoked.

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:02.570
The cash transfer network we set up 
for money laundering's been hit, too.

00:14:08.940 --> 00:14:11.940
What the hell?! Who's behind this?!

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:16.200
Would you look at that?

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:19.010
How much money do these guys make?

00:14:19.010 --> 00:14:21.220
That's national budget territory.

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:23.480
Good work, Ami.

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:26.380
Where do you wanna go?

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:27.420
Anywhere is fine.

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:30.220
All I really wanted was 
to get out of there.

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:33.090
Were you being confined?

00:14:33.090 --> 00:14:36.570
No. I was renting that room.

00:14:36.570 --> 00:14:38.100
Because it was safe and comfortable.

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:42.680
But after staying there too long, I was 
no longer able to leave under my own power.

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:48.450
So? How does it feel to be back in the 
outside world after all this time?

00:14:49.140 --> 00:14:50.090
It stinks!

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:53.270
That'd be the smell of gasoline.

00:14:53.270 --> 00:14:56.270
Cram it! Gas-powered cars are way more manly!

00:14:56.270 --> 00:14:57.830
How anachronistic.

00:14:57.830 --> 00:14:59.640
Says the samurai...

00:15:16.090 --> 00:15:18.140
The internet has everything.

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:21.630
Even services for just this kind of event.

00:15:50.790 --> 00:15:53.700
Beautiful Soup, analyze HTML—

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:54.690
Hey, Ami.

00:15:55.420 --> 00:15:56.210
What?

00:15:56.210 --> 00:15:59.720
You haven't eaten anything 
since you got here, have you?

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:01.700
Is that a problem?

00:16:01.700 --> 00:16:03.150
You'll die.

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:04.670
Yes, that is a problem.

00:16:05.240 --> 00:16:06.460
I'll eat.

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:07.350
Whoa there!

00:16:07.350 --> 00:16:08.800
I've got no strength...

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:11.050
You're not too bright, are you?

00:16:11.050 --> 00:16:13.950
Man, oh man. We're babysitting 
an overgrown baby.

00:16:14.470 --> 00:16:16.910
How long are we going to be playing house?

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:19.320
This girl would probably die 
if we left her on her own.

00:16:19.320 --> 00:16:21.860
We wait until Lupin's ready to go.

00:16:26.310 --> 00:16:29.390
Inspector Zenigata, 
the perimeter is in place.

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:31.360
Move in.

00:16:31.360 --> 00:16:33.520
We don't want to give Lupin any time to react.

00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:35.190
The cops?

00:16:35.190 --> 00:16:37.190
Look. Zenigata's with them.

00:16:37.190 --> 00:16:38.260
We've gotta run for it, Ami.

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:41.510
A smokescreen?!

00:16:44.640 --> 00:16:47.150
We left the water route open for a reason.

00:16:50.520 --> 00:16:51.500
Did we get him?!

00:16:52.750 --> 00:16:53.870
A decoy?

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:56.960
Don't think you've managed 
to evade me just yet.

00:17:02.860 --> 00:17:04.850
How did they discover the villa?

00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:07.470
Because you stand out way too much!

00:17:07.470 --> 00:17:09.990
Japanese people are not
 uncommon in France.

00:17:09.990 --> 00:17:11.620
That's not what I meant.

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:13.890
Zenigata?

00:17:13.890 --> 00:17:16.150
No, this is someone else.

00:17:16.150 --> 00:17:18.160
I wasn't even speeding!

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:19.970
You weren't speeding <i>yet</i>, you mean.

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:21.050
Exactly!

00:17:49.370 --> 00:17:50.480
Goemon!

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:51.500
Understood.

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:04.010
Have a nice day!

00:18:06.840 --> 00:18:08.150
Those vehicles are out of reach.

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:09.920
You give up too easily!

00:18:49.320 --> 00:18:51.850
Aw, my Fiat...

00:18:51.850 --> 00:18:55.280
Save the goodbyes for later, Lupin.

00:19:03.310 --> 00:19:06.790
Gotta wonder how people keep finding us.

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:08.160
The fault is not mine.

00:19:08.640 --> 00:19:11.560
I've confirmed that it's not 
a transmitter, either.

00:19:15.170 --> 00:19:16.300
<b>Welcome</b>

00:19:15.170 --> 00:19:16.300
<b>Mr. Ohno</b>

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:20.990
I got our tickets to Dusseldorf.

00:19:20.990 --> 00:19:23.460
Doesn't this scene strike you as odd?

00:19:33.030 --> 00:19:35.500
Hey, you seeing this, Jessica?

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:37.280
What are you doing, kid?

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:38.770
It's the Lupin Game!

00:19:38.770 --> 00:19:39.830
"Game"?

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:40.540
Look.

00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:47.950
Hunting down the greatest 
thief of our time: Lupin III.

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:50.080
There's only one rule.

00:19:56.080 --> 00:19:58.380
There are over a hundred 
million registered users...

00:19:58.380 --> 00:20:00.720
Even if only 10% of that 
number remain active,

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:03.390
that means ten million 
people on Lupin's trail.

00:20:06.440 --> 00:20:11.790
Oh, wow. Looks like you're the center of 
attention in a troublesome game, Lupin.

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:11.850
<b>Updates</b>

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:23.610
<b>Goemon's got such good posture!! 
He really is a samurai LOL</b>

00:20:23.610 --> 00:20:24.490
<b>That's Lupin III?</b>

00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:25.490
<b>The world's greatest thief HA</b>

00:20:25.530 --> 00:20:26.620
<b>Wasn't Lupin behind 
that thing a while back?</b>

00:20:26.660 --> 00:20:27.530
<b>Where's Lupin going?</b>

00:20:26.660 --> 00:20:27.530
<b>I hear he has hideouts around the world.</b>

00:20:26.660 --> 00:20:27.530
<b>Oh, I remember that!</b>

00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:30.040
<b>The airport. He's obviously flying.</b>

00:20:30.040 --> 00:20:32.540
<b>It's probably a group 
of 3 men and 1 woman.</b>

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:36.630
Some tickets were purchased 10 minutes ago
 for 3 men and 1 women.

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:38.920
They were headed for 
Dusseldorf on Berlin Air.

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:43.320
I get it.

00:20:43.320 --> 00:20:46.090
So everyone in the world is a cop now, huh?

00:22:16.430 --> 00:22:18.560
You hear about this Lupin Game?

00:22:18.560 --> 00:22:21.510
It's apparently all about 
finding Lupin III...

00:22:21.520 --> 00:22:25.030
And with people all over the 
world playing it on the internet,

00:22:25.030 --> 00:22:27.110
it's a real pain in my rear end.

00:22:27.110 --> 00:22:30.140
It's like everyone's a cop now.

00:22:30.510 --> 00:22:33.070
Well, catch me if you can.

00:22:33.070 --> 00:22:37.470
I didn't earn my rep by being the 
kind of guy amateurs can hunt down.

00:22:37.820 --> 00:22:39.820
And so, tune in next time 
for "The Lupin Game."

00:22:37.820 --> 00:22:44.840
<b>The Lupin Game</b>

00:22:39.820 --> 00:22:43.420
Man, being famous ain't easy!
